#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:1
msgid "Release 2.35.0 (2026-06-22)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:3
msgid "Highlights"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:5
msgid ""
"Sources are copied to the store more lazily [\\#3121](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/issues/3121) [\\#15711](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15711) "
"[\\#15920](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15920)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:7
msgid ""
"Historically, flakes source trees have been eagerly fetched to and evaluated "
"from the Nix store to ensure deterministic and hermetic evaluation, even if "
"the resulting store object is not used as a derivation input. This made the "
"implementation simpler, yet made flakes unusable in large repositories and "
"performed unnecessary writes to the store on each change to the source tree."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:9
msgid ""
"Since Nix 2.32, all I/O (excluding `path:` and `hg+:`\\-style inputs) for "
"reading sources during evaluation has been funneled to their original "
"filesystem location (or to the `~/.cache/nix/tarball-cache-v2` bare git "
"repository for tarball-based inputs). However, the source tree was still "
"fetched to the store -- primarily for computing the resulting content-"
"addressed store path. In most cases, (such as importing the `nixpkgs` "
"package set) this is not necessary."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:11
msgid ""
"Touching (and hashing the NAR serialisation of) the whole source tree is "
"unavoidable, since:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:13
msgid "In case of flake inputs, `narHash` integrity must be checked eagerly."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:14
msgid ""
"The `outPath` attribute of a flake must be known in advance, and for "
"backwards compatibility must be a content-addressed store path string with "
"[constant string context](../language/string-context.md#string-context-"
"constant) representing the flake source tree."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:16
msgid ""
"Even within the constraints imposed by backwards compatibility requirements, "
"there are several improvements that are achievable. To reduce the number of "
"copies performed, Nix now hashes the input without copying first, assuming "
"that the `.outPath` will not end up in a derivation attribute and thus would "
"never have to be actually fetched to the store. This comes at the slight "
"cost of doing more work in case the assumption is wrong, but results in less "
"work in typical use cases. The evaluator continues to behave as if the copy "
"was performed:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:18
msgid ""
"Flakes are still evaluated from the store, from the evaluator's point of "
"view."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:19
msgid ""
"`toString ./.` continues to produce a content-addressed store path string "
"without context."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:20
msgid ""
"Path resolution crossing trees located in the filesystem and in Nix's view "
"of it (with \"virtual\" overlays on top) continues to work. For example, the "
"flake source tree can contain a relative symlink pointing outside its "
"corresponding store object (though such usage is discouraged and makes "
"further improvements to laziness intractable)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:21
msgid ""
"Reading files from the flake's `outPath` continues to work. For example, "
"such code is well-formed and is not considered [IFD](../language/import-from-"
"derivation.md):"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:23
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"builtins.readFile ( /. + (builtins.unsafeDiscardStringContext self.outPath) "
"+ \"/flake.nix\" )\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:27
msgid ""
"Similar treatment has been applied to `builtins.fetchTarball`, which no "
"longer eagerly copies paths to the store. `builtins.storePath` now also "
"short-circuits on \"lazy-ish\" store paths and doesn't substitute unless "
"necessary."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:30
msgid ""
"This change is expected to significantly reduce disk usage required for "
"typical evaluations and results in ~2x speedup for fetching and unpacking a "
"nixpkgs tarball (either via `fetchTree`/flakes or via `fetchTarball`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:32
msgid ""
"Support FreeBSD `libjail` based sandboxing, add `x86_64-freebsd` to "
"installer [\\#9968](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/9968) [\\#13281]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/13281) [\\#15673](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/15673)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:34
msgid ""
"The FreeBSD build of Nix now supports build sandboxing via FreeBSD jails and "
"is enabled by default. A FreeBSD build has been added to the traditional "
"installer script. The beta rust-based installer is not yet supported. "
"FreeBSD support is not as well-tested as Linux or macOS, but is fully "
"capable of building packages and performing other tasks expected of Nix on "
"Linux."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:38
msgid "Improvements"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:40
msgid ""
"HTTP/3 (QUIC) support [\\#15961](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15961)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:42
msgid ""
"Nix can now fetch from binary caches and other HTTP(S) sources over HTTP/3 "
"(QUIC), controlled by a new [`http3`](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-"
"http3) setting (disabled by default). When enabled, Nix requests HTTP/3 and "
"transparently falls back to HTTP/2 or HTTP/1.1 for servers that do not "
"advertise QUIC. The setting only takes effect when linked against a "
"`libcurl` built with HTTP/3 support, otherwise it is ignored and Nix keeps "
"using HTTP/2 without warning or error."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:46
msgid "Enable it with:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:53
msgid "Or disable with:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:60
msgid ""
"Link mimalloc for faster evaluation [\\#15596](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/15596)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:62
msgid ""
"The `nix` binary now links [mimalloc](https://github.com/microsoft/mimalloc) "
"by default, replacing glibc's malloc for all non-GC allocations. This yields "
"a **5–12% wall-clock improvement** on evaluation workloads, ranging from "
"`nix-instantiate hello` to `nix-env -qa` and full NixOS configurations. The "
"allocator can be disabled at build time with `-Dnix:mimalloc=disabled`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:66
msgid ""
"The `revCount` attribute of the Git fetchers is now lazily computed and "
"passed-through as-is when explicitly specified [\\#15772](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/15772) [\\#14596](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/14596)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:68
msgid ""
"`revCount` and `lastModified` attributes passed to the Git fetcher are no "
"longer eagerly validated when explicitly specified."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:70
msgid ""
"When not explicitly specified, `revCount` is now also a thunk value and not "
"computed eagerly. This delays this (potentially) expensive computation until "
"the value is actually required."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:72
msgid ""
"Configurable file-transfer retry backoff with full jitter and `Retry-After` "
"support [\\#15023](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/15023) [\\#15419]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/15419) [\\#15449](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/15449)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:74
msgid ""
"File transfer retries (downloads and uploads) now use AWS-style \"full "
"jitter\" exponential backoff, treat HTTP 503 as rate-limited (same longer "
"delay as 429), and honor the `Retry-After` response header."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:77
msgid "Retry timing is configurable via new `nix.conf` settings:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:79
msgid ""
"[`filetransfer-retry-delay`](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-filetransfer-"
"retry-delay): base delay for transient errors"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:80
msgid ""
"[`filetransfer-retry-delay-rate-limited`](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-"
"filetransfer-retry-delay-rate-limited): base delay for 429/503"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:81
msgid ""
"[`filetransfer-retry-max-delay`](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-"
"filetransfer-retry-max-delay): per-attempt delay ceiling"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:82
msgid ""
"[`filetransfer-retry-jitter`](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-filetransfer-"
"retry-jitter): enable full jitter"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:84
msgid ""
"The existing `download-attempts` setting has been renamed to [`filetransfer-"
"retry-attempts`](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-filetransfer-retry-"
"attempts) to reflect that it applies to uploads as well as downloads. The "
"old name remains as an alias for backwards compatibility."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:87
msgid ""
"Per-substituter overrides are available as store reference parameters "
"([`retry-delay`](../store/types/http-binary-cache-store.md#store-http-binary-"
"cache-store-retry-delay), [`retry-delay-rate-limited`](../store/types/http-"
"binary-cache-store.md#store-http-binary-cache-store-retry-delay-rate-"
"limited), [`retry-max-delay`](../store/types/http-binary-cache-store."
"md#store-http-binary-cache-store-retry-max-delay), [`retry-attempts`](../"
"store/types/http-binary-cache-store.md#store-http-binary-cache-store-retry-"
"attempts)), e.g. `s3://my-cache?retry-attempts=8`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:89
msgid ""
"Improve daemon socket path logic for chroot stores [\\#15190](https://github."
"com/NixOS/nix/pull/15190)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:91
msgid ""
"The default daemon socket path now uses the per-store [`state`](../store/"
"types/local-store.md#store-local-store-state) directory whenever one is "
"defined, rather than always using the global [`NIX_STATE_DIR`](../command-"
"ref/env-common.md#env-NIX_STATE_DIR). This means [local chroot stores](../"
"store/types/local-store.md#chroot) each get their own socket path "
"automatically."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:94
msgid "Example:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:100
msgid "will now use a socket at:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:104
msgid "instead of"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:109
msgid ""
"Users who wish to serve or connect to a chroot store at the old location "
"will have to force the socket location:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:111
msgid ""
"When serving (running a daemon), use the new [`--socket-path`](../command-"
"ref/new-cli/nix3-daemon.md#opt-socket-path) flag:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:114
msgid "\"$NIX_STATE_DIR/daemon-socket/socket\""
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:117
msgid ""
"When connecting as a client, put the path in the [store URL](../store/types/"
"local-daemon-store.md):"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:119
msgid ""
"```\n"
"unix://$NIX_STATE_DIR/daemon-socket/socket\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:123
msgid ""
"Linux sandbox: also block `listxattr` syscalls [\\#15743](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/15743)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:125
msgid ""
"The Linux sandbox now also returns `ENOTSUP` for `listxattr`, `llistxattr` "
"and `flistxattr`, matching the existing treatment of `getxattr`/`setxattr`/"
"`removexattr`. This prevents host xattrs (e.g. `security.selinux`) from "
"leaking into builds and fixes tools such as `mkfs.ubifs` that probe xattr "
"support via `listxattr`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:128
msgid ""
"Support SCP-like URLs in fetchGit and type = \"git\" flake inputs [\\#14852]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/14852) [\\#14867](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/issues/14867) [\\#14863](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/14863)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:130
msgid ""
"Nix now (once again) recognizes [SCP-like syntax for Git URLs](https://git-"
"scm.com/docs/git-clone#_git_urls). This partially restores compatibility "
"with Nix 2.3 for `fetchGit`. The following syntax is once again supported:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:133
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"builtins.fetchGit \"host:/absolute/path/to/repo\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:137
msgid "Nix also passes through the tilde (for home directories) verbatim:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:139
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"builtins.fetchGit \"host:~/relative/to/home\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:143
msgid "IPv6 addresses also supported when bracketed:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:145
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"builtins.fetchGit \"user@[::1]:~/relative/to/home\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:149
msgid "`builtins.fetchTree` also supports this syntax now:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:151
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"builtins.fetchTree { type = \"git\"; url = \"host:/path/to/repo\"; }\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:155
msgid ""
"`nix flake check` now supports `--print-out-paths` [\\#13470](https://github."
"com/NixOS/nix/issues/13470) [\\#15476](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/15476) and `--out-link` [\\#13470](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"issues/13470) [\\#15476](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15476) defaulting "
"to not creating out links if the flag is not specified."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:157
msgid ""
"Added `--skip-alive` (and `--skip-live` alias for compatibility with Lix "
"users) option to `nix store delete` for collecting garbage within a closure "
"[\\#7239](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/7239) [\\#15236](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15236) [\\#15727](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/15727)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:159
msgid ""
"`nix store delete --recursive --skip-alive` can be used to collect garbage "
"within a closure, in which case it will only collect the dead paths that are "
"part of the closure of its arguments. The additional option `--also-"
"referrers` is added to support this mode, which allows referrers of paths in "
"the closure to also be deleted."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:162
msgid ""
"`builtins.getFlake` now supports path values [\\#15290](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/15290)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:164
msgid ""
"`builtins.getFlake` now accepts path values in addition to flakerefs. This "
"improves the usability of relative flakes, allowing you to write `builtins."
"getFlake ./subflake`. This change does not allow specifying paths that are "
"not already in the store (though they do not have valid store objects, i.e. "
"this will not force a copy if the flake has only been hashed -- and not "
"copied to the store). This may change in a future release."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:167
msgid ""
"`nix-profile.fish` and `nix-profile-daemon.fish` now use `$NIX_LINK` for "
"computing the value of `NIX_PROFILE` instead of `$HOME/.nix-profile` "
"[\\#14293](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/14293)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:169
msgid ""
"`nix` binary now exports symbols from C bindings [\\#15696](https://github."
"com/NixOS/nix/pull/15696)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:171
msgid ""
"This allows Nix plugins written against the C API to look up symbols "
"dynamically without linking to corresponding `libnix*c.so` libraries."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:173
msgid ""
"The computed Git LFS endpoint URLs have been fixed to follow the spec "
"[\\#15891](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15891) and memory usage of LFS "
"fetches has been decreased [\\#15912](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/15912)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:175
msgid ""
"We now verify that fetched Git LFS objects have the same OID as requested "
"[\\#15845](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15845)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:177
msgid ""
"Primop documentation now includes time complexity information [\\#14554]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/14554)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:179
msgid ""
"Improved documentation on store paths and derivation building [\\#14699]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/14699)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:181
msgid ""
"The [build hook](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-build-hook) is now killed "
"with `SIGTERM` instead of `SIGKILL` [\\#15105](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/15105)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:183
msgid ""
"Download/upload logs strip `userinfo` URL components [\\#15715](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15715)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:185
msgid "Content-addressed derivations changes"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:187
msgid ""
"The experimental content-addressed (CA) derivation feature has undergone a "
"significant change to how build traces (formerly called \"realisations\") "
"are identified. This changes the binary cache endpoints for realisations and "
"the daemon/nix-serve protocol (gated behind a daemon protocol feature flag)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:190
msgid ""
"Realisations keyed by store path instead of hash modulo [\\#11897](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/11897) [\\#12464](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/12464)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:192
msgid ""
"Previously, a build trace entry (realisation) was keyed by the hash modulo "
"of the derivation. In simpler terms, derivations transitively depending on "
"distinct fixed-output derivations with the same `outPath` would share a "
"realisation."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:194
msgid ""
"Now, build trace entries are keyed by the regular derivation store path (`."
"drvPath`) plus the output name. For example, instead of:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:200
msgid "The key is now:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:206
msgid ""
"Removed support for \"deep\" realisations [\\#15289](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/15289)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:208
msgid ""
"Previously the build trace (set of \"realisations\") contained entries for "
"both unresolved and [resolved](../store/resolution.md) derivations. Now, it "
"contains entries exclusively for resolved derivations. For now, unresolved "
"derivations will be resolved from these underlying build trace entries. This "
"is slower, but has the benefit of making build trace entries stateless and "
"self-describing --- making sharing realisations easier between stores."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:213
msgid "This change necessitates changes to the binary cache format:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:215
msgid ""
"The directory for build traces moved from `realisations/` to `build-trace-v2/"
"`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:216
msgid ""
"File paths changed from `realisations/<hash>!<output>.doi` to `build-trace-"
"v2/<drvName>/<outputName>.doi`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:217
msgid ""
"The JSON format of build trace entries is now split into `key` and `value` "
"objects:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:220
msgid "\"key\""
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:221
msgid "\"drvPath\""
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:221
msgid "\"abc...-foo.drv\""
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:222
msgid "\"outputName\""
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:222
msgid "\"out\""
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:224
msgid "\"value\""
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:225
msgid "\"outPath\""
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:225
msgid "\"xyz...-foo\""
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:226
msgid "\"signatures\""
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:226
msgid "\"keyName\""
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:226
msgid "\"cache.example.com-1\""
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:226
msgid "\"sig\""
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:226
msgid "\"...\""
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:230
msgid ""
"Previously, these were flat objects with a string `id` field like "
"`\"sha256:...!out\"`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:231
msgid "The deprecated `dependentRealisations` field has been removed."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:233
msgid ""
"The build trace entries stored in the local SQLite database no longer have "
"any foreign key references to store objects. This is because the build trace "
"entries for resolved derivations that may have been deleted need to be "
"preserved, otherwise the outputs of other unresolved derivations will be "
"effectively forgotten. GC for the build trace is not yet implemented due to "
"the lack of a clear default policy."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:237
msgid ""
"Structured signature for realisations and `path-info` [\\#15009](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15009)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:239
msgid ""
"[Signatures](../protocols/json/signature.md) in JSON formats are now "
"represented as structured objects with `keyName` and `sig` fields, rather "
"than colon-separated strings. `nix path-info --json --json-format 3` opts "
"into the new version for this command. JSON parsing accepts both the old "
"string format and new structured format for backwards compatibility."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:243
msgid "This format is also used for the build trace entries in binary caches."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:245
msgid ""
"`nix realisation` command has been renamed to `nix store build-trace` "
"[\\#16000](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/16000) [\\#15948](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15948)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:247
msgid "Build performance improvements"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:249
msgid ""
"Make post-build-hook asynchronous [\\#15406](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"issues/15406) [\\#15451](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15451)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:251
msgid ""
"The [`post-build-hook`](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-post-build-hook) "
"now runs asynchronously, without blocking the build event loop. Dependent "
"builds are not started until the hook finishes, but multiple hook instances "
"are now launched concurrently -- up to the [`max-jobs`](../command-ref/conf-"
"file.md#conf-max-jobs) limit."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:254
msgid ""
"zstd compression now emits multi-frame output and uses less memory [\\#15550]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15550)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:256
msgid ""
"zstd-compressed NARs are now written as a sequence of independent 16 MiB "
"frames instead of a single large frame. This lays the groundwork for "
"parallel decompression in a future release without requiring caches to be "
"repopulated, and significantly lowers peak memory use during compression (e."
"g. from ~600 MiB to ~100 MiB for a 1 GiB store path)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:260
msgid ""
"The output remains standard zstd and is decoded unchanged by existing Nix "
"binaries and the `zstd` CLI; compression ratio is effectively unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:262
msgid ""
"Per-frame compression now uses up to 4 worker threads. For zstd this is the "
"new default: the [`parallel-compression`](../store/types/http-binary-cache-"
"store.md#store-http-binary-cache-store-parallel-compression) store setting "
"defaults to `true` when `compression=zstd` (it remains `false` for other "
"compression algorithms like `xz`). Set `?parallel-compression=false` to opt "
"out."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:265
msgid ""
"More parallelism for binary cache uploads [\\#15957](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/15957)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:267
msgid ""
"Uploads of NARs now start without waiting for all references to be uploaded. "
"Also, NARs are now uploaded in order of descending (decompressed) NAR size. "
"The closure invariant is still maintained by copying `.narinfo` in a "
"topologically sorted order."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:271
msgid ""
"The derivation build scheduler memory usage reduction and performance "
"improvements [\\#15611](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15611) [\\#15695]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15695)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:273
msgid ""
"Memory usage of the derivation build scheduler has been improved to allow "
"more state sharing. Inefficiencies leading to quadratic complexity of "
"scheduling build/substitution jobs have been addressed. Scheduling resources "
"are allocated more sparingly and freed earlier to reduce peak consumption."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:277
msgid ""
"These improvements amount to ~2-8x less `nix-daemon` memory usage for "
"typical workloads and more in larger derivation graphs, not accounting for "
"short-lived allocations used during substitution."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:279
msgid ""
"Notably, the current architecture of the build scheduler gets proportionally "
"slower on Linux with larger heaps as derivation \"builder\" processes are "
"`fork`\\-ed directly from the Nix process, which blocks the builder event "
"loop for the duration of the `fork`. Thus, smaller heap of `nix-daemon` "
"translates into faster build startups."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:281
msgid ""
"Concurrent path substitutions and eval-time fetches of the same inputs now "
"run only once [\\#15555](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15555) [\\#15644]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15644)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:283
msgid ""
"This avoids redundant work in case multiple Nix processes try to substitute/"
"download the same resource concurrently."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:285
msgid "`.narinfo` lookups in binary caches are more concurrent"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:287
msgid ""
"Querying the existence and path metadata in binary caches is now more "
"asynchronous. Operations like `nix path-info` on large closures are faster "
"and more efficient. The build scheduler event loop now doesn't block on `."
"narinfo` queries, which improves performance with passthru binary caches."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:290
msgid "Bug fixes"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:292
msgid ""
"Fix hash collision between store paths with self-references and their zeroed-"
"out equivalents [\\#15837](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/15837) "
"[\\#15931](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15931)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:294
msgid ""
"When computing the hash of a NAR with self-references, Nix zeroes out the "
"self-references but also hashes their positions. The latter was accidentally "
"lost in Nix 2.17.0, which meant a NAR with self-references could hash to the "
"same store path as an otherwise-identical NAR in which some of the self-"
"references had been zeroed out."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:297
msgid ""
"This release restores hashing the positions of self-references. As a "
"consequence, content-addressed store paths derived from self-referential "
"NARs will differ from those produced by Nix 2.17 through 2.34. This affects "
"users of the experimental `ca-derivations` features, as well as users of "
"`nix store make-content-addressed`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:301
msgid ""
"C API: Fix `EvalState` pointer passed to primop callbacks [\\#15300](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15300) [\\#15383](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/15383)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:303
msgid ""
"The `EvalState *` passed to C API primop callbacks was incorrectly pointing "
"to the internal `nix::EvalState` rather than the C API wrapper struct. This "
"caused a segfault when the callback used the pointer with C API functions "
"such as `nix_alloc_value()`. The same issue affected `printValueAsJSON` and "
"`printValueAsXML` callbacks on external values."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:307
msgid ""
"GitHub fetcher now validates URL parameters [\\#15304](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/issues/15304) [\\#15331](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15331)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:309
msgid ""
"The `github:` fetcher now validates URL parameters, and will error if an "
"invalid parameter like `tag` is provided."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:311
msgid ""
"Fixed a bug where keep-outputs and keep-derivations can interfere with "
"delete commands [\\#15776](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15776)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:313
msgid ""
"Setting [`keep-derivations`](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-keep-"
"derivations) to `true` and trying to delete a derivation with realised "
"outputs would previously fail. Same with [`keep-outputs`](../command-ref/"
"conf-file.md#conf-keep-outputs) and trying to delete an output that still "
"has derivers. These options no longer affect the deletion commands, and are "
"now documented as such."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:317
msgid ""
"S3 substituters fall back to the URL's region for STS WebIdentity auth "
"[\\#15594](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15594)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:319
msgid ""
"When authenticating to an S3 binary cache via STS WebIdentity (EKS IRSA, "
"GitHub Actions OIDC), Nix now uses the `?region=` parameter from the S3 URL "
"as a fallback for the STS endpoint region if neither `AWS_REGION` nor "
"`AWS_DEFAULT_REGION` is set. Previously, IRSA setups that exported "
"`AWS_WEB_IDENTITY_TOKEN_FILE` and `AWS_ROLE_ARN` but no region would fail "
"with a misleading \"IMDS provider\" error."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:322
msgid ""
"S3: restore STS WebIdentity and ECS container credential providers [\\#15507]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15507)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:324
msgid ""
"Nix 2.33 replaced the S3 backend's `aws-sdk-cpp` credential chain with a "
"custom chain built on `aws-c-auth`. That chain omitted two providers, "
"breaking S3 binary cache access in container workloads:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:327
msgid ""
"**STS WebIdentity** (`AWS_WEB_IDENTITY_TOKEN_FILE`, `AWS_ROLE_ARN`, "
"`AWS_ROLE_SESSION_NAME`) -- used by EKS IRSA, GitHub Actions OIDC, and any "
"`sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity` federation."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:328
msgid ""
"**ECS container metadata** (`AWS_CONTAINER_CREDENTIALS_RELATIVE_URI`, "
"`AWS_CONTAINER_CREDENTIALS_FULL_URI`) -- used by ECS tasks and EKS Pod "
"Identity."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:330
msgid ""
"The typical symptom was a misleading IMDS error (`Valid credentials could "
"not be sourced by the IMDS provider`), because IMDS is the last provider "
"tried after the correct one was skipped."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:332
msgid ""
"Both providers are now part of the chain, ordered to match the pre-2.33 "
"behaviour. As in both the old and new AWS SDK default chains, ECS and IMDS "
"are mutually exclusive: when container credential environment variables are "
"set, IMDS is skipped."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:335
msgid ""
"HTTP 401 and 407 responses from binary caches are no longer treated as "
"missing files [\\#15877](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15877)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:337
msgid ""
"Nix no longer treats `Unauthorized` and `Proxy Authentication Required` HTTP "
"codes as an indication of a missing file. This used to be the case because "
"AWS S3 returns 403 `Forbidden` for missing objects in unlistable buckets. "
"401/407 were accidentally included and this workaround is now tightly scoped "
"to 403 responses."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:339
msgid ""
"Fixed `nixbld` gid in `/etc/group` in the Linux build sandbox when user "
"namespaces are not supported [\\#15131](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/15131)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:341
msgid ""
"Store garbage collection is now more robust [\\#15992](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/15992) [\\#15720](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15720) "
"[\\#15616](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15616)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:343
msgid ""
"Fixed deadlock for hash-mismatching fixed-output derivations [\\#15874]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15874)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:345
msgid ""
"`nix-copy-closure` no longer ignores `--include-outputs` flag [\\#15896]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15896)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:347
msgid "Fixes to `recursive-nix` experimental feature"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.35.md:349
msgid ""
"Prior to this release, internal datastructures used to implement this "
"feature were not used in a thread-safe manner. Threads handling daemon "
"connections are now reaped promptly, fixing resource leaks."
msgstr ""

